            "selectCount": 1,
            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><div><div class=\"notes-title\"><strong>Absence from work</strong></div><p>Absence may be frequent or occasional.</p><p class=\"sub-head\">Main factors involved</p><ul><li>the {{31}} of employees (e.g. females are likely to have responsibility for children)</li><li>employees' {{32}} (but the evidence is inconclusive)</li><li>the {{33}} of the organization (absenteeism may be acceptable)</li><li>the type of work (higher absence among employees in {{34}})</li><li>the {{35}} of an employee's work group</li></ul><p class=\"sub-head\">Public sector versus private sector</p><ul><li>public sector has higher absence levels</li><li>possible explanation — the public sector is less {{36}}</li><li>systems may be more bureaucratic because of {{37}} factors (e.g. state controls)</li><li>more recent literature suggests public sector organisations usually: <ul><li>— have a {{38}} workforce</li><li>— have more female and more older employees</li><li>— provide {{39}} for longer, with fewer restrictions</li><li>— are less likely to {{40}} employees</li></ul></li></ul></div>",
            "maxWords": 1
          }
        ]
      }
